<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Port Harcourt is the operating centre of Nigeria's oil and gas service economy, and the rotating equipment load that comes with it is unlike anywhere else in the country. Within Rivers State you find heavy duty gas turbines on co-generation duty, condensing and back pressure steam turbines, aeroderivative packages driving gas compression, and diesel and gas generator sets running everything from Trans-Amadi factories to Onne logistics bases. Our field teams work on that population directly, from combustion inspections and borescope surveys through to full rotor overhauls and alignment of complete trains.</p><p>What makes this environment demanding is not only the number of machines but the conditions they run in. Humid estuarine air off the Bonny River channel, salt carry near the coast and the particulate loading residents know as soot all load intake filtration, foul compressor blading and stress generator insulation faster than at an inland site. We scope each job around measured condition rather than a generic interval copied from a manual, and the reasoning goes into the written proposal before any work starts. <a href="/power-plant-audit-nigeria/">Book a plant assessment</a> or request a technical proposal to begin.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Do in Port Harcourt</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">Services for Port Harcourt Plants</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Gas turbine combustion and hot gas path inspections</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Borescope led inspection, combustor and transition piece work and hot gas path change out, planned around your Rivers State turnaround window. Associated gas with variable heating value, liquid carryover and sulphur content shortens hot end life, so we set scope on equivalent operating hours and fired starts rather than the calendar.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Steam turbine and co-generation overhauls</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Rotor lifts, blade and diaphragm inspection, gland and labyrinth seal renewal, journal and thrust bearing work, governor and trip system proving on the back pressure and condensing sets used across Eleme and Trans-Amadi process plants. Full scope detail sits on our <a href="/steam-turbine-overhaul-nigeria/">steam turbine overhaul</a> page.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Industrial generator maintenance and load bank proving</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Planned maintenance, alternator electrical testing, control and AVR work and resistive load bank proving for standby and prime rated sets across Port Harcourt, Onne and Oyigbo. Standby sets that idle through the dry season and then carry full load in a wet season outage need proving under load, not a no load test run. See <a href="/generator-maintenance-nigeria/">generator maintenance</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Compressor trains and rotating equipment services</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Laser alignment, field and workshop balancing, vibration diagnostics, dry gas seal and bearing work on the centrifugal and reciprocating packages that dominate Rivers State flow stations and gas processing sites. Driver and driven machine are treated as one train, which is covered under <a href="/rotating-equipment-services-nigeria/">rotating equipment services</a>.</p>
      </div>
</div>
<style>
